    "graph_40_layer_max_ms": 0.13298,
    "graph_40_layer_median_ms": 0.12331,
    "scope": "Free whole final six or seven Engram tasks including their internal gaps, plus the three mean tasks. Keep all gathers and their ordering, coefficient work, HcPre, and unrelated boundaries. Use the most favorable DP arrival and the largest observed 40-layer graph span on every eligible ordinal. Fixed-work conditional envelope, not a physical ceiling on a different pipeline."
  },
  "rank_window_graph_branch_witnesses": 112,
  "assumptions": [
    "Native matched separate vs joint: same early Y, same original late full HcPre, same TP8 gather/order or same local-Q schedule, same cache, same rank and round. Use the change in last group readiness, charge coefficient lateness over the original attention slack, retain losing comparisons, reuse costs on 34 direct layers. Translate each old DP arrival by that arm’s readiness change versus stock/gather, then apply the differential at the new reference skew. Verify the same request remains the P90 owner under the absolute timing intervals of every compared arm. These are synthetic native measurements transferred to historical requests, not a separate vs joint service A/B.",
    "Erase-all-exposed-lateness affects only the late coefficients; assume unchanged early clocks and no shared-resource interference. This is a conditional ceiling on improvement from this dependency, not all savings possible from a coefficients-only kernel. Existing service producer calls full HcPre on the aux stream and returns only outputs [1:].",
    "Traffic cases hold expert layout, schedule, attention collectives and weights fixed. Give the new producer the original BF16 result after rounding, and retain its global write for the delayed attention HcPost. Debit omitted read/write bytes against each historical task once using the per-size large-copy rates (M3 uses their median). Rate factors 1 and 2 represent alternative payload vs total-transfer conventions. Ignore tiling, spills, weight projection cost changes, launches and caches. Benefits from on-chip handoff require locality across old kernels. This estimates exposed traffic only.",
    "Ordinary direct Post can emit Y because previous FFN Pre already provided external premix. Direct joint two-read case also assumes the coefficient path consumes the same on-chip residual tile. Mean and Y have different coefficients and need their original orders/rounding. The mean output and gather remain. Preserve all three HcPre coefficient outputs and both RMSNorm outputs if live. Keeping only unrounded Post is incorrect.",
    "Engram layers 1 and 14 use the post-update residual, not the previous Post input. Six typed trailing operations and an optional TensorMove cover the entire profiled q in the measured shapes. Fuse the two casts to FP32, value slice, scaled multiply, add and BF16 round, preserving separate FP32 arithmetic, gate/mask, positions and slice-write aliasing. Add the weighted Y path only from the final updated BF16 rows. An uncaptured partial prefix needs an original-tail path. First layer lacks an upstream FFN Post; last FFN Post belongs to M08.",
    "The branch union takes one credit per original task or byte edge, includes both residual reads for all 39 post-initial layers and the optional auxiliary branch savings. Per layer use extrema across TP then recorded DP join bounds, sum prompt carriers and recompute request maxima. Graph and ordinary pricing assumes the same branch arrangement, traffic fully exposed, no mandatory graph writeback copy, and original step counts; ordinary eager copy priced both ways. Other readers or contention can hide or reverse gains. These are fixed-load estimates, not model-wide hardware ceilings."
  ],
